# Cloudflare reads this out of the asset directory. `public/` is copied into
# `out/` verbatim by `next build`, so this ships as `out/_redirects`.
#
# These two lived in next.config.ts `redirects()` until the static export.
# `output: 'export'` drops that config with a warning rather than an error,
# and the first of these is not cosmetic: without it there is no
# `out/index.html` at all and the bare domain returns 404.
#
# Limits: 2,000 static rules, 100 dynamic, 1,000 chars per line.

# `/` has no language, so it cannot render. 302 rather than 301 because the
# choice of default locale is a product decision that may change, and a
# cached permanent redirect would outlive it in browsers.
/          /ko            302

# The feed was unprefixed before locales existed. 301 because that move is
# settled — this one is permanent on purpose.
/feed.xml  /ko/feed.xml   301
